      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": false,
        "si_used": true,
        "procedure": "[Co2(μ-OH2)(O2CtBu)4]·(HO2CtBu)4 (100 mg, 0.1 mmol) was dissolved in CH3CN (8 mL). Diethanolamine (deaH3; 11 mg, 0.1 mmol) was added with stirring, followed by tBuPO3H2 (14 mg, 0.1 mmol) and NEt3 (40 mg, 0.4 mmol). Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (90 mg, 0.2 mmol) was then added and the mixture was stirred overnight at room temperature. The solution was filtered and the filtrate was kept at 4 °C for slow evaporation. Purple block crystals formed within 3–4 days and were collected by filtration, washed with cold CH3CN, and dried in air.",
